{
  "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
  "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Eric Schnapper)",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Vicky Crawford reported to city officials that she had been repeatedly harassed by the board's director of employee relations, her conduct was protected by section 704(a) of Title VII. It is protected first by the first clause of section 704(a), which is known as the opposition clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Case 06-1595, Crawford v. The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, Tennessee. Mr. Schnapper."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus)",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think this case is best resolved under the opposition clause, and that clause does not require employees to utter magic words of opposition or to initiate the interview in which they express opposition to unlawful conduct. Rather, the clause is satisfied when a reasonable person would understand that the employee has objected to sexual harassment in the workplace."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Facts that would constitute unlawful activity. What about facts that -- I mean, many of these cases, of course, are he-said/she-said cases, and what about the facts that you are reporting confirm one side or the other?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BLATT: The participation clause is much broader coverage. It could -- it would cover anyone who participates in the investigation, whether or not they oppose the practice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: You think -- you think the conduct in this case is also covered by the participation clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "EEOC",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0001-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BLATT: It's not in their compliance manual; it's in our amicus brief, but it is the EEOC's position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can you think of any other situation in which the law says that a person who testifies or provides information is protected against retaliation only if that person gives testimony of a particular type or gives a statement of a particular type?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What -- what more could Ms. Crawford do to make it clear that she opposes what was alleged in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Young",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YOUNG: Congress chose to use the word \"oppose,\" Your Honor. That's why the short --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Young, even under your definition, why is not the statement that's made in this case, \"get the hell out of my office,\" wouldn't that be opposition even under your statement, under your definition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Young",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "An -- an employer's internal sexual harassment investigation is not an investigation under this title."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why wouldn't this fall within the participation clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Young",
      "case_id": "2008-06-1595",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a5b5e97411bbcefd003e82121c4825e66b247eb805bd05ca046a2312878ffe5a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a5b5e97411bb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "as a result of this sexual harassment investigation when her subordinates were interviewed and they provided testimony regarding how she was running her office, and that eventually got to the finance department of the government, which hired an outside auditor which went in and generated all this evidence at great expense to the metropolitan government to hire this outside auditor. That's where the evidence was developed to terminate Ms. Crawford six months after the statement to the investigators."
    },
    {
